diff --git a/packages/python-sdk/PARITY.md b/packages/python-sdk/PARITY.md
index 5408c5e..ac2608e 100644
--- a/packages/python-sdk/PARITY.md
+++ b/packages/python-sdk/PARITY.md
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ JS `Run`/`StreamRun` → Python `Run`/`StreamRun` (+ `AsyncRun`/`AsyncStreamRun`
 | ---------------------- | ---------------------------- |
 | `Box` / `EphemeralBox` | `Box` / `EphemeralBox` (+ `Async*`) |
 | `Run` / `StreamRun`    | `Run` / `StreamRun` (+ `Async*`) |
+| `RunCancellationReceipt` | same (frozen dataclass in Python) |
 | `BoxError`             | `BoxError`                   |
 | `inferDefaultProvider` | `infer_default_provider`     |
 | `runCustomHarness`     | `run_custom_harness`         |
@@ -103,7 +104,8 @@ statics `create`, `from_snapshot`, `get_by_name`, `delete_boxes`,
 - Polling loops (2s/300s) in `create`, `from_snapshot`, `snapshot`.
 - `is_agent_configured`: `bool(data.agent)` on `create`; `bool(data.model)` on `get`/`from_snapshot`.
 - `Run.logs()`: epoch→ISO, **lower-bound-only** time filter.
-- `Run.cancel()`: swallows endpoint errors, always sets `cancelled`.
+- `Run.cancel()`: preserves the void/None contract and delegates to the shared at-most-once cancellation request.
+- `Run.requestCancel()` / `request_cancel()`: returns an immutable accepted/failed request receipt while leaving authoritative run status unchanged.
 - `files.download` destination: `./{basename}` | `./workspace` | `./{basename(cwd)}`.
 - 3-mode run request: file paths → multipart, base64 objects → JSON `files`, else plain JSON.
 
